-----Original Message-----
From: Sean Turner <sean@sn3rd.com>
Sent: Friday, October 16, 2026 6:54 AM
To: TLS List <tls@ietf.org>
Subject: [EXTERNAL] [TLS] Early IANA allocation for draft-ietf-tls-trust-an=
chor-ids

Hi! After a request from and discussions with the authors of draft-ietf-tls=
-trust-anchor-ids [1], the chairs would like to determine whether there is =
consensus to request an early code point assignment; see [2] about the earl=
y allocation process. The code point in question is for 'trust_anchors' in =
the TLS ExtensionType Values registry, see Section 12.1 of the I-D. As note=
d in [3], implementers have been using a value chosen at random and it has =
been stable since the initial draft. Please let the list know by 30 October=
 2023 if you support this early allocation.

NOTE: A new registry is defined in Section 12.3 of the I-D, but we cannot a=
sk for early creation of a registry.

Cheers,
spt (for the chairs)

[1] https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids/
[2] https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc7120/
[3] https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/tls/vD37D986i5YtFFvfLfkcte_WSxk/
